OL,3,GNEWSAMy autistic son could be trapped
OL,4,Ain the house if we lose our disabled
OL,5,Aparking bay
OL,6,
OL,7,FAn autistic teenager could lose his
OL,8,Findependence if his family's on-street
OL,9,Fparking bay is taken away, his mother
OL,10,Ffears.
OL,12,FClaire Gray, a full-time carer for her
OL,13,F16-year-old son Jack, said the bay -
OL,14,Fwhich is different to a blue badge
OL,15,Fspace - has changed his life.
OL,17,FJack is prone to running away and has
OL,18,Fdamaged neighbours' cars in the past,
OL,19,Fmeaning the family fear for his safety
OL,20,Fwithout it.
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,434,430,260,140,0,100
